#: ../../source/docs/common-3d-mapping.rst:35
#: 70d757c631e149108b59700ce85597b9
msgid "Sample Mission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3d-mapping.rst:40
#: 04bc85b692b84661983663e5b0931c06
msgid "A good 3d rendering can be accomplished with 60 ~ 100 still pictures. There should be at least 65% overlap between consecutive pictures but aiming for 80% or even higher is recommended.  The aerial photographs can also be combined with photos taken from the ground."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3d-mapping.rst:45
#: 5b9b8c4d74c641b59dd68fd46f3c75b5
msgid "The altitude of the mission depends upon the subject.  For large flat areas, flying 40m ~ 80m above the surface should provide very detailed images (and thus a detailed final product) but for buildings flying higher (i.e. 100m above the building) reduces distortion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3d-mapping.rst:50
#: 3125be49e9804c19b816cc46ebb270cf
msgid "It is recommended to fly a mission that is made up of parallel tracks with each track between 25m and 100m apart.  The higher the vehicle, the wider apart the tracks can be.  In general you should aim for 65% overlap in pictures from adjacent tracks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3d-mapping.rst:55
#: e05969af11f746bdb75a5276989b2a8f
msgid "The camera shutter needs to be triggered throughout the mission (i.e every 2 to 5 seconds or at regular distance intervals).  Many cameras include a feature to take pictures at regular time intervals. If not, then a camera shutter release method must be implemented via a relay control, see :ref:`common-camera-shutter-with-servo` for example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3d-mapping.rst:60
#: 9e8bc0a4f0bc4cbfb1b47dcc6507743e
msgid "A mission to accomplish this would include some or all of these commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3d-mapping.rst:63
#: 2469f9af3dfc462483e4d3dcac00b8eb
msgid "**TAKEOFF** - will cause the vehicle to climb straight to the target altitude provided in the \"Alt\" column (normally in meters)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3d-mapping.rst:66
#: 565716ff95604e7d88cb6f339facfa3a
msgid "**WAYPOINT** - provide as many waypoints as required to fly over the scene in a grid pattern.  Altitude should be entered in the \"Alt\" column.  Adding \"1\" to the \"Delay\" columns will cause the copter to momentarily stop at each waypoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3d-mapping.rst:71
#: 3ca439d025d847f9a4cc1bb119c11c2f
msgid "**DO_DIGICAM_CONTROL** will cause the camera shutter to be pushed once immediately if the autopilot has been connected using a servo.  This command takes no arguments and like other \"do\" commands it executes immediately after the preceding waypoint command begins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3d-mapping.rst:76
#: 7f2502c705054b0a9341d89c1a23b325
msgid "**DO_TRIGG_DISTANCE** is the same as do-digicam-control (above) except the camera shutter will trigger every X meters.  Where X can be defined in the first column labelled \"Dist (m)\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3d-mapping.rst:80
#: 3fdbf24410f94743b2d3c2912f2644ff
msgid "**RETURN_TO_LAUNCH** should be the last command in the mission so the vehicles returns home."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3d-mapping.rst:83
#: b9360c7c2e0f4661bc6d500f30ca7622
msgid "**DO_SET_ROI** can be used to point the nose of the vehicle and gimbal at a specific point on the map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3d-mapping.rst:90
